"The postoperative pathology reveals a Gleason 3+4 (ISUP grade group 2) and pathological stage pT2c. A positive surgical margin was documented, which is an adverse finding. Counterbalancing this is the absence of extraprostatic extension and the finding that \"the seminal vesicles were not invaded.\" Lymphovascular invasion was absent. Nodal status is documented as \"no lymph nodes were removed,\" meaning pNx does not establish node-negative disease, which widens uncertainty regarding nodal involvement. Preoperative PSA is not recorded, and postoperative PSA is also not recorded, meaning biochemical recurrence cannot be assessed. The documented findings of positive margins are adverse, while the lack of seminal vesicle invasion and absence of lymphovascular invasion are reassuring. Information regarding postoperative PSA and its trajectory is crucial for revising the prognosis. The fixed estimated horizon is 42.43 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 25.46–59.40 months; its coverage has not been validated."
